@using GameTownApp.Services
@inject MetadataRelinkService Relink

@*
    The sidebar's re-link entry, shown only when there is something to re-link.

    Re-linking is optional by design — migration 007 carried every game across with its images already
    local, so a library that never opens the tool renders correctly forever — and on an install created
    after the move to IGDB there is nothing it could possibly do. A permanent link to a screen whose
    only answer is "Nothing to re-link" reads as an unfinished chore, so the link is absent until the
    count says otherwise.

    A COMPONENT rather than a few lines in NavMenu, and specifically so that it can sit inside the
    Admin branch of AuthorizeView: nothing here is instantiated until authorization has resolved, so an
    anonymous visitor never fires an admin-only request that would come back 401. The route itself is
    untouched — /metadata-relink still loads if it is typed or bookmarked.

    The count is read once, when the sidebar is built. After the last pairing is applied the link
    lingers until the next page load; the page it leads to says "Nothing to re-link" by then, which is
    a better price than a shared-state service for a moment that happens once per install. NavMenu
    makes the same trade for its search box.
*@

@if (candidates > 0)
{
    <NavLink class="gt-nav__link" href="metadata-relink">
        <span class="bi bi-arrow-repeat" aria-hidden="true"></span> Re-link metadata
    </NavLink>
}

@code {
    private int candidates;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            candidates = await Relink.GetCandidateCount();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // Nothing renders, and that is the right failure: this link is an offer, not a control
            // anyone is waiting on, and an error message in the sidebar would be louder than the
            // link it replaced. The page remains reachable by URL.
        }
    }
}
